docker compose
------------
Docker Compose is a tool used to create and manage multiple Docker containers together using one YAML file, usually docker-compose.yml or compose.yaml.

Without Docker Compose
Suppose your application has:
Frontend → React container
Backend → Java/Python container
Database → MySQL container
You would need to run multiple docker run commands separately.

With Docker Compose You define everything in one file:

services:
  frontend:
    image: my-frontend                               frontend → service name
    ports:                                           my-frontend → image name
      - "3000:3000"

  backend:
    image: my-backend
    ports:
      - "8080:8080"

  database:
    image: mysql
    environment:
      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: secret

Then: docker compose up -d
Docker Compose will create and start all three containers.

docker compose up -d   Create and start containers in background.
docker compose ps      See Compose containers.
docker compose logs    See logs.
docker compose stop    Stop containers.
docker compose start    Start stopped containers.
docker compose down     Stop and remove containers/network created by Compose. This removes: Containers,Compose-created network
    It does not remove images or named volumes by default.
    If you also want to remove volumes: docker compose down -v
docker compose pull     Pull the images specified in the Compose file.
docker compose restart   Restart the services.

docker compose -f myapp/docker-compose.yml ps       you can see by Outside the folder — also possible
docker compose -f myapp/docker-compose.yml logs      You can stay outside and tell Compose exactly where the file is using -f.
