depends_on 
--------------
 means  “Start this service after the service I depend on has been started.”
Your startup order
Because of depends_on, Compose starts them in this order:
database
   ↓
backend
   ↓
frontend

when you run :  docker compose up -d
Compose understands:
database must be started first
        ↓
backend can be started
        ↓
frontend can be started

Important point ⚠️
depends_on does NOT mean the application is fully ready.
For example:

database container starts
        ↓
MySQL is still initializing
        ↓
backend container starts

the database container has started, but MySQL might still be preparing the database.
So depends_on mainly controls service startup order, not "wait until the service is completely ready."
For true readiness, you can use a healthcheck with condition: service_healthy.

why we starting first what is the udse of
